"Workflows for work that runs the business Mistral AI has released 'Workflows', an orchestration layer to stably operate enterprise AI processes. Workflows provides durability, observability, and fault tolerance for AI-based processes, helping them operate reliably in production environments. Developers write workflows in Python and publish them to Le Chat so that anyone in the organization can trigger them. Execution is fully traceable and auditable, and complex business processes can be deployed to production within days. Speaking of Voxtral Mistral AI has unveiled 'Voxtral TTS', a lightweight (4B parameters) text-to-speech (TTS) model optimized for multilingual speech generation. A lightweight model with 4B parameters, providing low latency and cost-effectiveness, optimized for enterprise voice agent workflows Supports 9 languages ​​including English, French, German, Spanish, Dutch, Portuguese, Italian, Hindi, and Arabic Beyond simple reading, it is possible to create a natural voice that reflects the speaker's personality and cultural nuances such as intonation, rhythm, and emotional expression. As a result of human evaluation, it showed superior naturalness compared to ElevenLabs Flash v2.5 and equivalent voice quality to v3. Introducing Forge Mistral AI has launched ‘Forge’, a system that helps companies build custom AI models using internal proprietary data. Forge learns from a company's internal documents, code base, and operational records to create an AI model that deeply understands the company's domain knowledge and work environment. Supports learning approaches across the model lifecycle, including pre-training, post-training, and reinforcement learning, to align models to your unique operational goals and policies. By taking direct control of models and data in their own infrastructure environment, companies can gain strategic autonomy and address intellectual property and compliance issues. Introducing Mistral Small 4 Mistral AI announces Mistral Small 4, a new general-purpose model that integrates inference, multimodal, and agent coding capabilities. It is a hybrid model that integrates the functions of Magistral for reasoning, Pixtral for multimodal, and Devstral for coding. Efficiency is improved by activating 4 of the 128 expert (MoE) models per token, and it supports 256k context windows. The reasoning_effort parameter allows users to adjust response speed and level of reasoning as needed. Mistral AI partners with NVIDIA to accelerate open frontier models Mistral AI has decided to participate in NVIDIA's 'NVIDIA Nemotron Coalition' as a founding member to jointly develop and advance open source frontier AI models. Mistral AI has joined the 'NVIDIA Nemotron Coalition', NVIDIA's global initiative for AI open source models, as a founding member. We plan to jointly develop an open source frontier AI model by combining Mistral AI's model architecture with NVIDIA's computing resources and technology. As part of the collaboration, Mistral AI has released the Mistral Small 4 model for developers and researchers. Anthropic blocks all public access to Claude Fable 5, Mythos 5 following US government order — what enterprises should do In compliance with the U.S. government's national security mandate, Anthropic has blocked global public access to its top AI models, Claude Fable 5 and Mythos 5. Due to the U.S. government's emergency export control directive, Anthropic has immediately suspended access to the Claude Fable 5 and Mythos 5 models. This measure is believed to be related to the 'Pliny the Liberator' model jailbreak that exploited a security vulnerability, but Anthropic sees this as excessive regulation. This incident shows how operationally risky it can be for companies to rely on a single AI model, and suggests the need to diversify AI models. Windows 11 finally finds files when you type two characters instead of three Microsoft's June 2026 update improves Windows 11's search functionality, allowing you to search for files with just two letters and prioritizing local files over web results. The minimum number of characters to enter for Windows 11 search has been reduced from 3 to 2, making it easier to find files with short names. When displaying search results, the user's local files have been improved to be placed at the top rather than web results or AI suggestions. This improvement is part of the 'June Patch Tuesday' update, which contains a total of 200 security patches, including 33 critical vulnerabilities and 3 zero-day vulnerabilities. OpenAI is under investigation by 42 state attorneys general, days after filing for its IPO Immediately after OpenAI applied for the IPO, it was subject to a comprehensive investigation, including data policy, marketing, and safety, by attorneys general from 42 U.S. states. A coalition of 42 U.S. state attorneys general launches large-scale investigation into OpenAI New York State issues subpoenas requesting submission of materials related to advertising, user data, minor protection and internal policies This investigation was conducted just days after OpenAI applied for an IPO with a corporate value of $852 billion, so it is expected to pose a significant legal risk. US government orders Anthropic to kill Fable 5 and Mythos 5 in unprecedented AI model recall The U.S. government ordered Anthropic to discontinue service of the Fable 5 and Mythos 5 models due to national security and the possibility of model jailbreak. The U.S. government issued an export control directive on June 12, ordering Anthropic to suspend service access for the Fable 5 and Mythos 5 models. This is an unprecedented mandatory service suspension due to national security concerns related to reported model jailbreaks. Anthropic complied with the order, but publicly protested that this measure was excessive and warned that if similar cases were applied across the industry in the future, it could completely stop deploying AI models. Andrew Yang thinks the next big startup opportunity is lowering the cost of living Andrew Yang argues that business models that reduce essential living expenses will be a big opportunity for next-generation startups amid economic changes brought about by AI. Andrew Yang was inspired by Mark Cuban's 'Cost Plus Drugs' and emphasizes the value of a business model that returns profits to customers. In a situation where AI threatens jobs, I believe that lowering essential living costs such as housing, education, groceries, and communications will be an important differentiator for startups. The MVNO service he founded, 'Noble Mobile', is a practical example of trying to fill policy gaps with market logic through cost-saving benefits. Anthropic’s safety warnings may have just backfired — the government has pulled the plug on its most powerful AI Anthropic is strongly opposing the government's move to halt the use of its AI models due to potential jailbreak vulnerabilities found in them. The government has halted use of Anthropic's most powerful AI model, citing potential jailbreak risks. Anthropic argued that recalling commercial models distributed to hundreds of millions of people based on narrow vulnerabilities would be excessive. Anthropic officially expressed its dissatisfaction with the government's decision on its blog. My yard is dying, so I made an app for that We introduce the ‘vibe-coding’ experience of using AI models to quickly develop a personal gardening app without any professional coding knowledge. Users have attempted to develop Android apps using Gemini to organize gardening tasks and diagnose plant problems. After entering detailed prompts, the AI ​​built the app and even took care of bug fixes. It shows the potential of ‘vibe coding’, which allows complex projects to be implemented simply by interacting with AI, even without coding knowledge. Anthropic cuts off Fable 5 and Mythos 5 access following government order Anthropic has blocked all foreign access to its Fable 5 and Mythos 5 models in response to government national security orders. Anthropic blocks access to Fable 5 and Mythos 5 models to all foreigners inside and outside the United States in compliance with export control guidelines The government cited national security issues as the reason, but Anthropic said it had not been provided with specific threats or evidence. Anthropic claims that the vulnerabilities in the model are minimal and are at a general level found in other AI models such as GPT 5.5. Apple’s new AI photo editing tools mostly work, for better and worse iOS 27のデベロッパーベータ版で導入されたAppleの新しいAI写真編集機能の評価についての記事です。 iOS 27のデベロッパーベータ版に「Clean Up」、「Extend」、「Spatial Reframing」という3つの新しいAI写真編集機能が導入されました。 Clean Upツールはクラウドベースのモデルを採用することで、以前のデバイス内モデルよりも遥かに高い性能を実現しました。 新機能はiPhoneのフォトアプリに大きな転換点をもたらしますが、Extend機能など一部には制限や課題も存在します。 The future of Hollywood isn’t feeding prompts into vanilla gen AI models We cover the impact of generative AI on the Hollywood film industry and the proper use of AI technology identified at the Tribeca Film Festival. Most AI video models are limited to producing videos that lack visual consistency and are of low quality. At the Tribeca Film Festival, successful cases emerged where generative AI was used creatively in collaboration with the planning of human artists, rather than simply generating prompts. Works like Dear Upstairs Neighbors show that AI can produce more persuasive results when used with artistic intent rather than a technical focus. Anthropic Disables Claude Fable 5 and Mythos 5 After US Government Order Anthropic has completely discontinued its latest AI models, Claude Fable 5 and Mythos 5, in response to U.S. government export control orders. On June 12, 2026, the U.S. Department of Commerce issued an export control order for Claude Fable 5 and Mythos 5 for national security reasons. Anthropic found it difficult to block foreigners' access to models in real time, regardless of whether they were inside or outside the U.S., so it suspended model services for all users to ensure compliance. Anthropic is refuting the government's actions regarding the 'jailbreak' risk raised by the government, saying that the vulnerability is common and exists in other public models. Moonshot AI Releases Kimi K2.7-Code: a Coding Model Reporting +21.8% on Kimi Code Bench v2 Over K2.6 Moonshot AI has launched 'Kimi K2.7-Code', a new coding expert agent model designed for complex software engineering tasks. Kimi K2.7-Code has significantly improved coding performance compared to the previous model, K2.6, and adopts a Mixture-of-Experts structure. Optimized for software engineering tasks, planning, tooling, and debugging are performed in multiple steps. Reduces inference token usage by 30%, improving cost efficiency and processing speed, and supports a context window of 256K tokens. A Coding Implementation on Spatial Graph Neural Networks for Urban Function Inference Using city2graph, OSMnx, and PyTorch Geometric We provide a tutorial on building a spatial graph neural network (GNN) to infer city functions using city2graph, OSMnx, and PyTorch Geometric. Build an end-to-end spatial graph learning pipeline that collects real city data from OpenStreetMap or, if not available, uses synthetic data. Describes how to model urban environments by engineering spatial features and creating a variety of proximity graph structures. We implement a GNN-based inference process to predict Points of Interest (POI) categories from spatial structures using the GraphSAGE model. How to set up local coding agent on macOS How to build and optimize a coding agent in a local environment for Internet failures in a macOS environment. Built a local coding agent using llama.cpp and the Gemma 4 26B-A4B GGUF model in the Apple M1 Max environment. By applying speculative decoding and MTP draft model, the generation speed was improved by 24% (58.2 tok/s -> 72.2 tok/s). As a result of testing various model execution methods (llama.cpp vs MLX) in the macOS environment, the combination of llama.cpp and MTP showed the best performance. Malware developers add nuclear and biological weapons language to spyware Cases have been reported where malware developers exploit the LLM's safety denial function and bypass security scanners by inserting phrases related to nuclear and biological weapons into spyware. Attackers are exploiting LLM's excessive safety sorting to create a 'secondary blind spot' that interferes with security analysis. LLM's knowledge of nuclear weapons is already public information, and may be overestimated for the sake of AI company reputation management rather than actual risk. Biological hazards can be a relatively more real threat than nuclear weapons. Oracle reduces free usage limits for Ampere A1 instances Oracle has reduced the free usage limit for its cloud service, Ampere A1 instances, to half the previous amount. Ampere A1 instance free usage limit changed from up to 4OCPU + 24GB to 2OCPU + 12GB. If you exceed your limit, you may be charged standard fees or have your service suspended. AMD EPYC-based instances are excluded from this scale-down. Moonshot AI has released Kimi K2.7-Code. Moonshot AI has launched 'Kimi K2.7-Code', an agent-centric open weight coding model that significantly improves coding performance and reduces inference token consumption by 30%. An agent-driven model for planning, code modification, tool execution, and debugging for software engineering tasks. The MoE structure has 1 trillion (1T) parameters, activates 32B parameters, and supports 256K context windows. It showed excellent performance in coding performance benchmarks, surpassing the existing model K2.6 and even surpassing Claude Opus 4.8 in some items. “Can’t I just upload it to ChatGPT?” This article analyzes the relationship between the use of AI as a translation tool and the expertise of human experts from the perspective of a freelance translation expert. Professional translation is not a simple conversion, but a specialized field that requires understanding the context, localization, and maintaining consistency. AI such as ChatGPT can play an auxiliary role as a tool, but the accuracy of the results must be rechecked by humans. The value of experts should not be undervalued due to the misunderstanding that AI can replace them. Unprofessional Coauthor Behavior with Hallucinated References [D] This article emphasizes the importance of verifying references through a case where a co-author added false references created using AI to the paper, resulting in the paper being withdrawn. A co-author added false references using AI just before the deadline, submitted it without properly verifying it, and the paper was withdrawn. The scientific content of the paper was excellent and received an acceptance grade, but the researcher's reputation was damaged due to errors in the references. It is emphasized that references added by unreliable co-authors must be verified directly. Anomaly Detection vs Classification for Visually Similar Cancer vs Mimics? [P] A technical question for researchers about the optimal model approach (anomaly detection vs. supervised learning classification) to distinguish between visually very similar cancer samples and counterfeit samples (mimics). Researchers are designing a model to detect specific cancers Voice data is morphologically very similar to cancer data, making it difficult to distinguish. Seeking advice from experts on which model is more effective: anomaly detection or supervised learning classification. Derivative-Free Neural Network Optimization: MNIST Case [R] This is an example of applying the technique (MDP), which directly optimizes a neural network without differential information without using gradient descent or backpropagation, to the MNIST classification problem. Direct optimization of a neural network with 25,450 parameters without gradient information. Using the MDP optimization technique, we recorded superior verification accuracy (93.7%) and test accuracy (93.4%) than the existing Adam method. Through 1,000,000 function evaluations, we confirmed successful convergence in a high-dimensional search space without gradient-based learning. Threads of underground fungal networks are long enough to reach beyond the Solar System Research has shown that the vast network of mycorrhizal fungi that exist underground around the world plays an important role in regulating climate by sequestering carbon. The total length of the world's underground mycorrhizal fungal network amounts to 110 quadrillion kilometers. This mycelial network lives symbiotically with plants, sequestering carbon underground in return for providing nutrients such as phosphorus and nitrogen. Contributes to curbing global warming by sequestering 1 billion tons of carbon each year. SPUN (Society for the Protection of Underground Networks) researchers used machine learning to map this network globally for the first time. Anthropic shuts down Fable, Mythos models following Trump admin directive Anthropic has suddenly suspended service for Mythos 5 and Fable 5 models, which were just released, in accordance with the U.S. government's export control guidelines. Anthropic immediately disabled Mythos 5 and Fable 5 models for all customers following receipt of the U.S. Department of Commerce's export control directive. This measure is a security response to concerns raised about jailbreaks that bypass cybersecurity, chemical, and biological safeguards. The U.S. government has called for a moratorium on model launches until strengthening the national security system is complete. The wearable health boom is creating a data overload for doctors - what happens next Addresses the data overload problem experienced by doctors as the vast amount of data generated by wearable health devices is not integrated with existing systems in the medical field. Wearable devices constantly generate health data such as heart rate and sleep patterns, but the current medical system is designed for one-time treatment, making it difficult to efficiently accommodate this. Doctors feel limited in clinically utilizing the vast amount of data brought in by patients, and point out that much of the data has unclear clinical value. Experts expect that AI technology will be an alternative that can solve this data overload and support clinical decisions. I switched to Alpine Linux, and it's a crazy-fast distro with only one caveat This is a review of how to use Alpine Linux as a desktop operating system and its pros and cons. Alpine Linux is very lightweight and optimized for security, so it is mainly used for container deployment, but can also be used for desktops. It does not provide a desktop environment by default and does not even include sudo or bash, so users have to set it up manually, which is inconvenient. Although the setup process may be a bit difficult for beginners, it provides a lightning-fast desktop experience for users who value simplicity and security. The best VPN routers of 2026: Expert tested and reviewed We introduce the best VPN router families tested and selected by experts in 2026 and explain the features of each product. Setting up a VPN on your router is beneficial for security and privacy by protecting all connected devices at the same time. A VPN lets you hide your IP address, bypass geo-restrictions, and access content from other countries. ZDNET has updated the guide to reflect the latest market conditions, excluding out-of-stock products and adding new products such as Synology RT6600ax and ASUS ZenWiFi BQ16. Visa is handling AI-prompted transactions for OpenAI - but can you trust it? Visa and OpenAI are partnering to build an infrastructure to enhance the security of payment transactions performed by AI agents. Visa's 'Trusted Agent Protocol' is integrated with interfaces such as OpenAI's Atlas and ChatGPT Shopping. Users can directly control the payment authority of AI agents by setting safeguards such as consumption limits and approval procedures. This collaboration aims to bring AI-based commerce into the mainstream and provide a safer and more reliable payment environment for consumers and businesses. Watching sports at home? I'd change these 4 soundbar settings for the most optimal audio Here are four ways to optimize your soundbar settings to improve audio quality when watching sports at home. The room calibration function allows you to optimize soundbar performance to suit the size of the room and furniture placement. If commentary during a sports game is difficult to hear due to background music or crowd noise, it is effective to reduce the bass setting. Use the Dialogue enhancement feature to emphasize the midrange and make your voice sound clearer. You can use night mode or add rear speakers to reduce noise or experience three-dimensional sound. WebMCP Standard Proposal for Agentic Web Actuation Now Available in Chrome (Origin Trials) Google has released WebMCP, a new standard that helps AI agents reliably interact with websites, as an Origin trial in Chrome 149. WebMCP allows websites to explicitly expose tools such as JavaScript functions or HTML forms to AI agents, allowing the agents to reliably simulate user behavior. There is a lower possibility of errors than existing DOM scraping or screen analysis methods, and token consumption and delay time can be reduced. Developers can use the Declarative API (HTML properties) or the Imperative API (JavaScript) to define tools for the AI ​​agent to use. U.S. Orders Anthropic to Suspend Fable 5 and Mythos 5 Access for Foreign Nationals The U.S. government has ordered Anthropic to block foreign users' access to its AI models Fable 5 and Mythos 5, citing security concerns. Anthropic has temporarily suspended access to the Claude Fable 5 and Mythos 5 models in response to the U.S. government's foreign access restriction order. The US government has raised concerns that the models could be 'jailbroken' and used to weaponize cyberattacks. Anthropic has taken steps to strengthen security, stating that its Mythos-class model has the ability to quickly convert vulnerabilities into attack code. Fable 5, Missos 5 overseas service suspended...US executive order to block foreigners The U.S. government issued an executive order blocking foreign access to Antropic's 'Fable 5' and 'Missos 5' for national security reasons. The U.S. Department of Commerce judged national security risks and announced export control guidelines based on reports of successful jailbreaks by competitors. Antropic counters that the measure is an excessive response based on the potential and non-universal possibility of a jailbreak. This incident is expected to have a negative impact on Antropic's service expansion and listing ahead of its IPO. Moonshot AI unveils open source coding model ‘Kimi K2.7-Code’… “30% reduction in inference costs” Moonshot AI announced that it has released the open source coding model 'Kimi K2.7-Code' and has improved cost efficiency by reducing the use of inference tokens. Moonshot AI released the open source coding model 'Kimi K2.7-Code' on the 12th. Compared to the previous model, 'accident token' usage was reduced by 30%, reducing inference costs and improving coding performance. Although internal benchmarks showed performance improvement, experts pointed out that independent external benchmark verification was necessary. Xiaomi unveils open source coding agent ‘Mimo Code’… “Exceeding Claude’s code in a long-term workbook” Xiaomi has unveiled 'MiMo Code', an open source terminal-based AI coding agent optimized for long-term and complex programming tasks. It was designed around three axes: computation, memory, and evolution to solve the context loss problem that occurs during the long task process of existing AI coding agents. It has a ‘max mode’ that generates and evaluates up to five candidate solutions in parallel, and a ‘goal’ mechanism where a separate verification model checks the work. Continuity and performance of long-term tasks are ensured through a four-level memory structure and an 'evolution' function that periodically organizes and summarizes experiences. Google unveils natural language-SQL conversion technology 'Gemini-SQL2'... \"Accuracy exceeds 80%\" Google unveiled 'Gemini-SQL2', a next-generation technology that converts natural language into SQL queries, and announced that it recorded the industry's highest level of accuracy in the BIRD benchmark. Google introduced 'Gemini-SQL2', a natural language-SQL conversion technology based on 'Gemini 3.1 Pro'. It recorded an execution accuracy of 80.04% on the BIRD leaderboard, improving performance compared to existing models. It will be applied to various business data utilization environments, such as corporate revenue management and data engineering. Moonshot AI unveils ‘Kimmy Walk’… “Automating my PC document and web operations with 300 agent swarms” Moonshot AI has unveiled 'Kimi Work', a desktop AI agent that automates complex tasks through local file access and browser control on the user's PC. Provided as a standalone desktop app, easy for general users to install and use Complex, long-term tasks can be performed through the ‘Agent Swarm’ structure, which operates up to 300 sub-agents in parallel. Supports task automation by directly controlling the browser while maintaining the login session through WebBridge technology Antropic suspends 'Fable 5' service entirely due to U.S. government guidelines The U.S. government has completely banned foreign access to Antropic's high-performance AI models 'Fable 5' and 'Mythos 5' due to security threats and the possibility of jailbreak. Through export control guidelines, the U.S. government ordered access to Antropic's 'Fable 5' and 'Mytos 5' models blocked by all foreign nationals. Antropic has completely disabled the services of these models for all customers to comply with regulations. The government judged that the possibility of 'jailbreaking' the model could lead to a cybersecurity threat, but Antropic objected, saying it was an excessive measure. Antropic 'Claude Army' recognized as AI replacement for jobs is created Antropic officially recognized the possibility of AI replacing jobs and announced a youth paid fellowship program called ‘Claude Corps’ and an economic future research fund worth $200 million to alleviate this. Antropic provides AI utilization training and practical opportunities through the ‘Claude Corps’, a 12-month full-time paid fellowship for early career employees. $200 million will be invested into the 'AI Economic Future Research Fund' to study the economic impact of AI, supporting policy experiments and preparation of response measures. Instead of simply expressing 'job reconstruction', this is a strategy to strengthen the brand of a responsible AI company by directly acknowledging the possibility of job replacement by AI. Mind AI participates in Cheonan City’s urban safety network construction project Error 500 (Server Error)!!1500.That’s an error.There was an error. Please try again later.That’s all we know. Maum AI is participating in an environmentally adaptive, multi-purpose, on-device AI-based urban safety net project with Cheonan City to carry out a project worth 1.6 billion won. The quadrupedal robot 'HAECHI-02' is deployed to patrol and respond to disasters in vulnerable areas that are difficult to manage with fixed CCTV. We build a stable robot operating system that is not limited by the network through domestically produced AI semiconductors and VLA-based autonomous intelligence technology. Sparrow successfully completes ‘SAI 2026’… Presenting SW supply chain security strategy in the AI ​​era Sparrow presented a software supply chain security strategy in a development environment where AI and open source use is rapidly increasing through the annual event 'SAI 2026'. We diagnosed security threats occurring in the latest development environment centered on open source and AI coding. He emphasized the need to expand the scope of SBOM management to trace AI-generated code and verify its integrity. We proposed 'Sparrow MCP', which performs security verification from the point of code creation, and announced its official release. PCN participates in ‘STK 2026’… AI, XR, and space virtual convergence technology unveiled PCN participated in 'Smart Tech Korea 2026' and unveiled key R&D achievements in the fields of AI, XR, and space digital twin. We introduced ultra-low-latency XR cloud computing technology that allows high-quality XR content to be used even on low-end devices. We have unveiled a space digital twin control technology that implements satellite and space debris information in a real-time 3D virtual environment. We announced ‘OZai’, an AI agent solution that integrates corporate data and LLM to understand and execute goals on its own."